/_build/
/deps/
# Data, and not code: the memory of conversations, the inventory of sessions, the mark of sending.
# Formerly the source of the embedder lay here too — and silently did not get into
# the repository. Now priv/ holds only data, the code lives next to its own
# Dockerfile (embedder/embedder.py).
/priv/
*.beam
*.dets
erl_crash.dump
.env
# The CA of the egress filter. The private key (mitmproxy-ca.pem) lies here too — the one
# with which the filter signs the substituted certificates. A leak = the possibility
# to listen to the traffic of the agent. The folder is created by the filter itself at the first launch.
/certs/
# The real keys, laid out into files from .env by the deploy.sh script. As
# files, and not as variables: the hand reads out the environment of a container through the
# docker API (`docker top` with ps_args=wwaxe), while a mounting it does not.
/secrets/
# The Python cache from any folder: docker-filter, scripts, anything. It appears
# by itself on the import of a module, it has nothing to do with the repository.
__pycache__/
*.py[co]
